  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-IND176</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">increased capacity of constituents, including at the state level, to make social dialogue more influential and labour relations institutions and processes more effective</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ILO aims to galvanize constituent capacity and buy-in for strengthening social dialogue in traditional sectors/institutions, while promoting it in new sectors such as platform economy, renewable energy, etc. in India. It works closely with labour administrations of selected states in India to identify and remedy potential weaknesses in realizing their mandates related to labour dispute resolution. It enhances the understanding and supports the realization of effective mechanisms of collective bargaining, workplace cooperation and grievance handling in key sectors/states. In achieving these aims, the ILO promotes a gender-inclusive, non-discriminatory approach, capitalizing on the synergy ILO constituents and concerned stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
